{"id":"heyderabad","qid":"Q5749711","category":"city","type":"oikonym","names":{"az":"Heydərabad","ru":"Гейдарабад","en":"Heydarabad"},"coordinates":[48.41179,39.85685],"coordinatesSource":"wd","region":"mil-mugan","regionSource":"wp-az-regions","admin":[{"qid":"Q601105","az":"Saatlı rayonu","en":"Saatly District"}],"firstRecord":null,"period":null,"forms":[],"namedAfter":[],"etymology":[],"summary":{"az":{"text":"Heydərabad (əvvəlki adı: Qolovinovka) — Azərbaycan Respublikasının Saatlı rayonunun Dədə Qorqud kənd inzibati ərazi dairəsində kənd. 5 oktyabr 1999-cu il tarixli 708-IQ saylı Azərbaycan Respublikasının Qanunu ilə Saatlı rayonunun Dədə Qorqud kənd inzibati ərazi vahidi tərkibindəki Qolovinovka kəndi Heydərabad kəndi adlandırılmışdır.","truncated":false,"source":"wp-az"},"en":{"text":"Heydərabad (known as Golovinovka until 1999) is a village and municipality in the Saatly Rayon of Azerbaijan. According to the decision of the Milli Majlis of the Republic of Azerbaijan dated October 5, 1999, Dadli Gorgud village administrative-territorial unit of Saatli region was named Golovinovka village of Heydarabad.","truncated":false,"source":"wp-en"}},"images":[],"sources":[{"id":"wd","kind":"wikidata","title":"Wikidata Q5749711: Heydarabad","publisher":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5749711","licence":"CC0 1.0","retrieved":"2026-11-26"},{"id":"wp-az","kind":"wikipedia","lang":"az","title":"Heydərabad (Saatlı)","publisher":"Vikipediya (azərbaycanca)","url":"https://az.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Heyd%C9%99rabad_(Saatl%C4%B1)&oldid=8580421","pageUrl":"https://az.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heyd%C9%99rabad_(Saatl%C4%B1)","revid":8580421,"revDate":"2026-02-26","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved":"2026-11-26"},{"id":"wp-en","kind":"wikipedia","lang":"en","title":"Heydərabad","publisher":"Wikipedia (English)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Heyd%C9%99rabad&oldid=1377788719","pageUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heyd%C9%99rabad","revid":1377